      "cost": "Costs: n is the entry count, k the distinct-value count. Preprocessing takes O(n+k²): Counter reads n entries in O(n), sorting k distinct values takes O(k log k), and the compatibility matrix takes O(k²). Since k≥1, O(k²) absorbs sorting. For [2], six 2s and twelve 2s, k stays 1 but counting still reads 1, 6 and 12 entries; a conservative search bound is O(n·n!) time, still factorial. Depth n, O(k) counts and an O(k²) compatibility matrix give O(n+k²) auxiliary space. The simulation additionally stores every snapshot and ledger; those are not submission memory."
